  {
    "title": "One server is not enough",
    "body": "A single server reaches its limit at about 300 requests per second. Peak traffic is 900. You can make the server bigger (vertical scaling), but a machine has a ceiling and one failure takes everything down. Adding more identical servers (horizontal scaling) removes the ceiling, if the rest of the system can keep up.",
