  {
    "title": "Remove a broken server",
    "body": "The load balancer calls each server's health check every few seconds. A server that does not answer OK is taken out of rotation. Requests sent to it before the check notices are lost, so clients should retry safely. A short interval finds failures faster but adds checking load; a long one sends more requests to a dead server first.",
